{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_019JHATnNXa7cjoDRibMV6SF","type":"tool_result","content":"docs/paper/sections/analysis.tex:11:Three settings break this circularity: (1)~cross-coding-agent transfer (GB 0.967 on OH, where cmd\\_rep fires on 5.4\\% vs.\\ 65.5\\% of windows---LF memorization cannot explain this); (2)~instance isolation (removing 284 shared SWE-bench tasks changes cross-agent F1 by ${<}$0.1\\,pp, Table~\\ref{tab:instance_isolation}); (3)~gold validation (GB 0.839 vs.\\ MV 0.798, $p{<}0.001$; \\S\\ref{sec:gold_set}).\ndocs/paper/sections/experiments.tex:61:\\label{tab:main_results}\ndocs/paper/sections/experiments.tex:94:The probe is encoder-agnostic: three backbones all exceed 0.90 F1 (Appendix Table~\\ref{tab:encoder_ablation}), and a Transformer encoder is equivalent to GRU ($+$0.18\\,pp, $p{=}0.82$) on 5-step windows.\ndocs/paper/sections/experiments.tex:109:The three LFs occupy distinct temporal niches relative to stagnation onset (Table~\\ref{tab:lf_temporal}, Figure~\\ref{fig:lf_temporal} in Appendix~\\ref{sec:app_lf_temporal}): cmd\\_rep leads by 1.87 steps, file\\_diff is near-concurrent ($-1.20$), and outcome\\_bp lags by 6.70 steps (all pairwise $p{<}10^{-26}$).\ndocs/paper/sections/experiments.tex:132:\\label{tab:cmd_rep_ablation}\ndocs/paper/sections/experiments.tex:135:Removing cmd\\_rep drops macro-F1 by 29.4\\,pp (Table~\\ref{tab:cmd_rep_ablation}; McNemar $p{\\approx}0$) due to data volume collapse: cmd\\_rep expands training data ${\\sim}$10$\\times$ (4K$\\to$43K windows) while agreeing 100\\% with 2-LF labels on overlapping windows---purely a coverage contribution (Appendix~\\ref{sec:app_label_quality}).\ndocs/paper/sections/experiments.tex:141:Five label models---three temporal (TWV, HMM, Lag-HMM) and two generative (FlyingSquid, Snorkel MeTaL)---all fail to improve over majority vote (Table~\\ref{tab:temporal_models} in Appendix~\\ref{sec:app_tlm_results}); the best (TWV, $+$0.6\\,pp self-evaluated) degrades downstream probe F1 by 2.57\\,pp.\ndocs/paper/sections/limitations.tex:8:Silver-label evaluation dominates this study; while a 505-window gold set provides partial non-circular validation (\\S\\ref{sec:gold_set}), the primary metrics in Tables~1--5 remain silver-evaluated, and the structural RF's 0.995 macro-F1 reflects LF-reconstructibility rather than ground-truth detection accuracy.\ndocs/paper/sections/appendix.tex:21:\\label{tab:encoder_ablation}\ndocs/paper/sections/appendix.tex:41:\\label{tab:window_ablation}\ndocs/paper/sections/appendix.tex:61:\\label{tab:multiseed}\ndocs/paper/sections/appendix.tex:86:\\label{tab:cross_agent_cmdrep}\ndocs/paper/sections/appendix.tex:143:\\label{tab:feature_defs}\ndocs/paper/sections/appendix.tex:164:\\label{tab:instance_isolation}\ndocs/paper/sections/appendix.tex:171:Table~\\ref{tab:llm_extended} extends the zero-shot LLM-as-judge baseline (Table~\\ref{tab:main_results}) with chain-of-thought (CoT) prompting, few-shot examples, and an alternative model, all evaluated on the SWE-Agent conf${\\geq}$2 test set ($N{=}1{,}824$).\ndocs/paper/sections/appendix.tex:191:\\label{tab:llm_extended}\ndocs/paper/sections/appendix.tex:264:\\label{tab:temporal_models}\ndocs/paper/sections/appendix.tex:359:\\label{tab:lf_temporal}\ndocs/paper/sections/appendix.tex:414:\\label{tab:gold_batch1}\ndocs/paper/sections/appendix.tex:443:\\label{tab:feature_overlap}"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_011px2qzXanuBtKfZzqbMU3j","session_id":"4efa5a2a-e3e9-4e76-992e-c9082babf060","uuid":"5603369a-c448-4b68-95f6-4a128dea9b7c","timestamp":"2026-05-16T03:30:44.742Z"}
