{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Liu2pBmxXUSHaYsZfE9X5h","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t\\section{Related Work}\n2\t\\label{sec:related_work}\n3\t\n4\t\\paragraph{Process Supervision and Self-Reflection.}\n5\tPRMs assign step-level quality scores \\citep{xi2025agentprm,choudhury2025prm,fan2026agentrm}, building on process supervision \\citep{lightman2024letsverify,uesato2022processfeedback}, with benchmarks revealing long-horizon degradation \\citep{wang2026planrewardbench,li2026toolprmbench}.\n6\tSelf-reflection methods \\citep{shinn2023reflexion,yao2023tot,zhou2024lats} prompt agents to diagnose failures, but LLMs cannot reliably self-correct without external feedback \\citep{huang2024selfcorrect,kamoi2024selfcorrection}.\n7\tWe address a complementary question---\\emph{when} is the agent stuck---using external structural signals at window level, targeting real-time monitoring ($<$5\\,ms) without outcome labels.\n8\t\n9\t\\paragraph{Weak Supervision, Noisy Labels, and Label Leakage.}\n10\tData programming \\citep{ratner2016dataprogramming,ratner2019snorkel} enables dataset creation through labeling functions, extended via multi-task aggregation \\citep{ratner2019snorkelmetal}, triplet methods \\citep{fu2020flyingsquid}, sequential HMMs \\citep{safranchik2020linkedhmm}, multi-resolution LFs \\citep{sala2019multiresolution}, and benchmarked by WRENCH \\citep{zhang2021wrench}.\n11\tUnlike \\citeauthor{safranchik2020linkedhmm}'s NER results, temporal label models do not improve over majority vote in our low-conflict 3-LF regime (\\S\\ref{sec:temporal_label_models}).\n12\tOur silver labels connect to noisy label learning \\citep{han2018coteaching,li2020dividemix}; the structural feature--label overlap instantiates label leakage \\citep{kaufman2012leakage} and Goodhart's Law \\citep{manheim2018goodhart}, mitigated through cross-coding-agent evaluation, a gold set (\\S\\ref{sec:gold_set}), and active learning \\citep{settles2009active} for future expansion.\n13\t\n14\t\\paragraph{Agent Benchmarks and Monitoring.}\n15\tAgent evaluation spans diverse environments---general tasks \\citep{liu2024agentbench}, web navigation \\citep{zhou2024webarena}, interactive coding \\citep{yang2024intercode}, tool use \\citep{qin2024toolllm}, and debugging \\citep{tian2024debugbench}---creating demand for scalable monitoring.\n16\t\\citet{orlanski2026slopcodebench} document coding agent degradation; \\citet{chen2025monitoring} show sequence-level context is necessary; \\citet{kale2025weaktostrong} show weak monitors can oversee stronger agents; and \\citet{cemri2025multiagentfail,zhu2025agentfail} catalog systematic failure modes.\n17\tGuardrail frameworks \\citep{rebedea2023nemo,xiang2024guardagent} address safety but not progress.\n18\t\n19\t\\paragraph{Anomaly Detection, Process Mining, and Compute Efficiency.}\n20\tStagnation detection relates to sequential anomaly detection \\citep{chandola2009anomaly}, including deep log analysis \\citep{du2017deeplog,meng2019loganomaly} and runtime verification \\citep{leucker2009runtime}.\n21\tCycle detectors \\citep{george2025cycledetection,pipis2025reasoningloop} target structural repetition but miss semantically diverse stagnation; \\citet{liu2026trajad} train trajectory verifiers for broader anomaly detection.\n22\tOur structural features draw on process mining \\citep{vanderaalst2016processmining}; the success of hand-crafted features parallels classical findings for narrow detection tasks \\citep{liu2008isolationforest}.\n23\tEarly-exit architectures \\citep{teerapittayanon2016branchynet,schwartz2020righttool} and curriculum learning \\citep{bengio2009curriculum} reduce computation by adapting effort to instance difficulty---analogous to stagnation detection, where the goal is terminating unproductive agent computation.\n24\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jd5fi31Jun3QQkhFFUSeJ9","session_id":"4efa5a2a-e3e9-4e76-992e-c9082babf060","uuid":"8b665624-e1c8-4f4d-b150-b77830f837f9","timestamp":"2026-05-16T03:30:46.099Z"}
